preferred-citation:
  type: software
  title: "TCS formalizations: sunflowers, the metric TSP integrality gap, IP = PSPACE, Toda's theorem, and the PCP theorem"
  authors:
    - family-names: Lee
      given-names: Troy
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6912-2338"
  version: pcp-v0.1.0
  date-released: 2026-10-18
  doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23445994
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of the PCP theorem, NP = PCP(O(log n), O(1)). Every
  NP language has a verifier that uses O(log n) random bits and a constant
  number of queries, with perfect completeness and soundness 1/2, and whose
  polynomial running time is certified on Mathlib's Turing machines; the
  converse is also proved. The proof follows the algebraic construction of
  Amireddy, Behera, Srinivasan, Sudan and Willumsgaard for 3-coloring, without
  PCP composition, and adds a reduction from every NP language to 3-coloring.
  Its NP class is shown equal to Complexitylib's unchanged definition.
  Developed with AI assistance; original attribution is preserved for all
  vendored sources. This component is included in the TCS formalizations
  repository.
keywords:
  - computational complexity
  - PCP theorem
  - probabilistically checkable proofs
  - low-degree testing
  - formal verification
  - Lean
